          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 18:52:37.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanityn 43k and 45j",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanityn 43k and 45j\n\nsanityn 43k and 45j each run a race 100 times for each of two\nfail_locs. Every iteration spends about 2.4 s in CI, mostly in\nfour separate do_nodes calls to the MDS (clear its LRU, list\nunused locks, set fail_loc, clear fail_loc) plus a 0.5 s sleep.\n\nThe fail_locs are CFS_FAIL_ONCE with CFS_RACE, so the first\nrequest to arrive waits for the second on every iteration and\nthe race is hit each time. Run 25 iterations per fail_loc.\nDo the MDS side LRU clear and fail_loc set in one do_nodes, and\ndrop the diagnostic listing and the per iteration fail_loc\nclear, since ONCE has already fired; 45j now also resets\nfail_loc at the end, as 43k does.\n\nMeasured on a single node rocky9 VM, three runs each:\n43k 134, 131 s before and 30, 30, 30 s after; 45j 132, 132 s\nbefore and 30, 29, 29 s after.\n\nIn CI each averages about 490 s, with about 3860 runs of each\nper 30 days. At the same 77% reduction that saves about 375 s\nper test per run, or about 800 hours per 30 days in total.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=\"43k 45j\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ibcf3ec3dfa663fdbb6ef937a20a1b4d94699d37a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
